# The Vercel project's Root Directory is `micro_rag/web`, but that path is resolved
# relative to whatever the CLI uploads — so `vercel deploy` must be run from the REPO
# ROOT (running it inside micro_rag/web makes Vercel look for micro_rag/web/micro_rag/web
# and fail). Uploading from the root means everything outside the web app has to be
# excluded here.
#
# Without this file the CLI does NOT fall back to .gitignore in a useful way: a deploy
# from the root uploaded 1.6 GB and died on "File size limit exceeded (100 MB)", because
# data/ carries the 420 MB pipeline SQLite database. Measured 2026-08-17:
#   data/                       1,606 MB   <- the whole failed upload
#   micro_rag/web/node_modules    699 MB
#   micro_rag/web/.next           135 MB
#   .venv/                         12 MB
#
# Note that once this file exists it REPLACES the .gitignore fallback entirely, so
# node_modules and .next must be listed explicitly rather than assumed.

# The pipeline's own state and outputs — never needed to build the web app, and the
# single largest thing in the repo.
/data

# Local toolchains and agent/session state.
/.venv
/.git
/.pi-sessions

# Vendored Python scraper — pipeline-side only.
/vendor

# Dependencies and build output are produced by Vercel's own build, not shipped to it.
/node_modules
/micro_rag/web/node_modules
/micro_rag/web/.next

# Databases and archives should never be uploaded regardless of location.
*.db
*.sqlite
*.zip

# Local logs and transcripts.
*.log
/2026-*.txt
/dataset_chat.txt
